Physical models, conflicting similarity and scale effects (@fd-model-similarity: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @fluid-dynamics, #source "../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Mechanics-MIT-2-25.lingua#r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ", #source "../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18", #source "../sources/NCFMF-Fluid-Mechanics-Films.lingua#r_0RT6J26HJJ83MX74030JPEHQVP", #fluid-dynamics "Dominant-balances-small-parameters-and-singular-limits.lingua#r_7SWMXVAX4WWEGQPEDHHHNJT8AR") { r_4YXMPWTHM9X4WSM304JNBWVS37
**Read:** [Advanced Fluid Mechanics — MIT 2.25, Fall 2013](../sources/Advanced-Fluid-Mechanics-MIT-2-25.lingua#r_1ZVEYBFSRC755ASSQ2X87MD8VZ), dimensional analysis and physical modelling problems; [Lectures in Elementary Fluid Dynamics — James M. McDonough](../sources/Elementary-Fluid-Dynamics-McDonough.lingua#r_7F9FTDV2VV4P28PG16J5PJSK18), similarity and experimental modelling; [Fluid mechanics films and illustrated notes — NCFMF](../sources/NCFMF-Fluid-Mechanics-Films.lingua#r_0RT6J26HJJ83MX74030JPEHQVP), similarity, waves and low-Reynolds-number demonstrations.

A scaled experiment must preserve the dimensionless controls relevant to the conclusion. Matching geometry alone is insufficient. With the same liquid and gravity, reducing a free-surface model's length and matching Froude number changes Reynolds and Weber numbers; all three generally cannot remain unchanged at once.

State which forces dominate and estimate the unmatched terms. A model may still answer a bounded question if the mismatch has a demonstrated small effect. Surface roughness, inlet disturbance, wall compliance, gas content and measurement resolution can introduce additional scale effects.

Plan two model sizes or operating conditions that test the proposed similarity. Collapse the observations using declared scales and display where they fail to collapse. A fitted dimensionless curve does not prove that omitted physics is irrelevant beyond the observed range.

**Continue:** [Dominant balances, small parameters and singular limits](Dominant-balances-small-parameters-and-singular-limits.lingua#r_7SWMXVAX4WWEGQPEDHHHNJT8AR).

